{
  "info": {
    "name": "PayPal Commerce Agent — AI Café",
    "description": "Complete API collection for **AI Café**, an agentic-commerce prototype built for the PayPal AI Hackathon.\n\nThe agent prepares a shopping cart from natural-language intent, but the **server owns all prices** and a **human authorizes every PayPal payment**. The AI never touches money. A read-only PayPal **Ops Copilot** lets a merchant audit activity.\n\n**How to use**\n1. Import this collection and the `paypal-commerce-agent.postman_environment.json` file.\n2. Set `baseUrl` (default `http://localhost:3000`) — or your Render URL.\n3. Run folder **`0 · Authentication > Start session`** first. It mints a server-side session and stores `sessionId` + `sessionToken` for the rest of the run (collection-level Bearer auth uses them automatically).\n4. Then run any request, folder, or the whole collection in the Collection Runner.\n\n**Why some requests return 503**: `AI chat`, `Orders create`, and `Ops ask` require server-side secrets (an AI key, PayPal sandbox credentials, or the Ops key). On a fresh deploy without those, the API answers `503` by design — the collection's tests accept `200/201` *or* `503` so the run stays green. Set the secrets in your environment (or Render dashboard) to exercise the full flow.\n\nPrize context: this collection is the tryability surface for the **Postman** sponsor prize.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{sessionToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "orderId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "paypalOrderId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "opsKey",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "checkoutToken",
      "value": "PAYID-EXAMPLE",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "mcpSessionId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "mcpOrderId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 · Authentication",
      "description": "A session is server-issued and returned exactly once. Store it, then present `X-Session-Id` + `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on every protected call. The collection-level Bearer auth already does this for you.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Start session",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(201));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionId', j.sessionId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionToken', j.sessionToken);",
                  "pm.environment.set('sessionId', j.sessionId);",
                  "pm.environment.set('sessionToken', j.sessionToken);",
                  "pm.test('returns sessionId + sessionToken', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.sessionId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(j.sessionToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/sessions",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "sessions"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Mint a server-side session. Rate-limited per IP (30/hour on shared hosts) — reuse the cached token across a run."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "End session",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/sessions/current",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "sessions",
                "current"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Logout / reset the demo. Clears AI-prepared cart + conversation."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
